{"author":"John Wesley","book":"Notes on the Bible","chapter":636,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:wesley:2Chr.10","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"John Wesley","authorshipDateRange":"18th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Methodist","translator":null,"edition":"CCEL edition; source omits 2 Samuel 24","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"wesley","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"}},"originalBook":"2 Chronicles","sourceVolumeId":"wesley","source":{"id":"wesley","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/wesley/notes.html","title":"Notes on the Bible"},"title":"2 Chronicles 10","reference":"2 Chronicles 10","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"The people request Rehoboam to ease their grievances, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":2,"text":"1-5.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":3,"text":"Rehoboam rejecting the old mens counsel, by the advice of the young men answers them roughly, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":4,"text":"6-15.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":5,"text":"Ten tribes revolt, ver.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":6,"text":"16-19.","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":7,"text":"4.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":8,"text":"Grievous - It is probable, when Solomon had declined from God, that God left him to himself to act thus impolitically.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":4,"scriptureVerseEnd":4},{"verse":9,"text":"7.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":10,"text":"If thou be kind, &c. - Moderate counsels are generally best.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":11,"text":"Gentleness will do what violence will not do.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":12,"text":"Good words cost nothing but a little self-denial, and yet they purchase great things.","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":13,"text":"16.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":14,"text":"See to thine own house - When public affairs are in a ferment, violent proceedings do but make ill worse.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16},{"verse":15,"text":"Many have been driven to the mischief they did not intend, by being too severely dealt with.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":16,"scriptureVerseEnd":16}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"2 Chronicles","chapter":10}}